242. Valid Anagram
Given two strings s and t, return true if t is an anagram of s, and false otherwise.

Anagram means - consider word s , all letters of word s should be used to make word t. s.length()==t.length()

Explanation:

we have 2 string s and t.
put leeters of S with the frequency in the hashmap.
Iterate the leeters through t, and check if they are present in the hashmap of s.
if they are not present immediately return false.
Supose if they are present reduce their frequency in the map.
Now check if the frequency of letter of t is 0, if so remove the leeter from hashmap.
Finnaly outside check if map is empty... if map is empty its true cause all letters are present in t and they have bee crossed out.
else false

Code:
class Solution {
    public boolean isAnagram(String s, String t) {
        if(s.length()!=t.length()){
            return false;
        }

        HashMap<Character, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        for(char ch: s.toCharArray()){
            map.put(ch,map.getOrDefault(ch,0)+1);
        }

        for(char ch: t.toCharArray()){
            if(!map.containsKey(ch)){
                return false;
            }

            map.put(ch,map.get(ch)-1);
            if(map.get(ch)==0){
                map.remove(ch);
            }
        }
        
        if(map.isEmpty()){
            return true;
        }
        
        return false;
    }
}
